  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I got new headphones for my Samsung phone 2 days ago. It's the kind that have to plug into the charging port. They have disconnected a couple times because my charging cord is a bit beat up. This happened while I was playing V.R.chat. When this happened I got a pop-up asking if I wanted the app to use the headphones. I accidentally pushed no. All the sudden the headphones are convinced they are a charger with no power. It doesn't matter what fix I try, it doesn't matter whose phone they're plugged into. It just pops up as a charger that doesn't have power. I even get pop up on my phone questioning why it doesn't have power. I have no idea what else to do.",
